The vertex of a parabola ax² + bx + c is at x = -b/(2a). In this case, the quadratic is A = -W² + 20W. So, comparing to ax² + bx + c, a = -1, b = 20. Therefore, the vertex occurs at W = -b/(2a) = -20/(2*(-1)) = -20 / (-2) = 10. 

